OL,3,GNEWSAJohn Swinney defends #45,000
OL,4,Abusiness-class flights to World Cup
OL,5,
OL,6,FJohn Swinney has defended the use of
OL,7,Fmore than #45,000 of public funds on
OL,8,Fbusiness-class flights for him and two
OL,9,Fsenior aides to the World Cup.
OL,11,FThe first minister flew to Boston on 11
OL,12,FJune for Scotland's opening match,
OL,13,Fbefore taking part in trade talks in
OL,14,FKentucky three days later.
OL,16,FWhile he and two senior officials
OL,17,Ftravelled business class, Sports
OL,18,FMinister Maree Todd and several other
OL,19,Fofficials went to the US on
OL,20,Fsignificantly cheaper economy-class
OL,21,Fflights.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,422,420,260,160,0,100
